-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/3bb78ba1-722e-5bee-ad2e-257d0bb70a0b
-- title:
--   Functions regular off the q+1 ends are finitely generated (q=3)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with the hypothesis $q = 3$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell \mid M'$ is fixed. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, that is, $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; its residue field is written $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$.
--
--   Three fields of Laurent series occur. The field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ is the intermediate field of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\kappa$ over $\kappa$ generated by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`; $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, in the sense of `laurentBaseChange`, of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M' \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb Q$; and $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of intermediate fields.
--
--   A finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$ over $\kappa$ is given, and `hW` says that its members are exactly the elements of $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,\kappa$, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa \to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')$ lies in the set $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa$ of supersingular $j$-invariants. A member $s \in W$ is fixed.
--
--   Next, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degrees, and the compatibility clauses of that structure. The hypothesis `hR₀` identifies $R_0$ with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image under the coefficient map induced by $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read back as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ along $A \to \kappa$.
--
--   The remaining data are: a field $FSS$ which is a $\kappa$-algebra; a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ to $FSS$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ whose intersection with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $A$, together with a surjective residue map onto $FSS$ with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A \to \kappa$ and satisfying the rescaling clause `exists_smul_mem`); a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$; for each place $Q$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$ a subring $S_Q \subseteq \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, a ring homomorphism $\varphi_Q : A[X] \to S_Q$, a ring homomorphism $\chi_{0,Q} : S_Q \to \kappa$, and a set $D_Q$ of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   The hypotheses on these data are the following.
--
--   `h0`: some element of $FSS$ is transcendental over $\kappa$.
--
--   `h1` (compatibility of $R$ with $R_0$ at $s$): for every $f \in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ such that at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the $q$-expansion of $j$ (the element $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}\,\mathrm{jq}$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$) implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}\,f$, and such that the $R_0$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$: the image of $f$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is the image under $\kappa \to FSS$ of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$.
--
--   `h2` (level stability of $R$): for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, the pullback of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ equals $R.\mathrm{integers}$.
--
--   `hcard`: $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   `hpkg` (smooth-point packages off $N$; fourteen clauses, summarised here): for every place $Q \notin N$, the image of $A$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $S_Q$; $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_Q$ sends constants $C\,a$ to the images of $a$, and $\chi_{0,Q}\circ\varphi_Q$ sends $C\,a$ to the residue of $a$ and $X$ to $0$; for every $c \in A$ with zero residue there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_Q \to A$ fixing constants, reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$ and sending $\varphi_Q X$ to $c$; every $f \in S_Q$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and its residue there is the image of $\chi_{0,Q} f$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_Q X$ has $Q$-order $1$; the set $D_Q$ consists precisely of the rational places $P$ at which every $f \in S_Q$ is regular with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and for which $A.\mathrm{valuation}(P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f) < 1$ holds exactly when $\chi_{0,Q} f = 0$; each $\chi : S_Q \to A$ fixing constants and reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$ is realised by a unique $P \in D_Q$ via $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$; for $P \in D_Q$ the valuation subring of $P$ consists of the quotients $g/h$ with $g,h \in S_Q$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,h \neq 0$; a nonzero $f$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}\,f = 0$ for all $P \in D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by a nonzero constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and any $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ regular at every $P \in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$.
--
--   `hdisj`: for $Q, Q' \notin N$, if some place $P$ lies in both $D_Q$ and $D_{Q'}$ then $Q = Q'$.
--
--   `hcusp`: for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_Q$, the order at $P$ of the image in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of the $q$-expansion of $j$ is non-negative.
--
--   `heqv` (equivariance of the ends and of the discs): for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$: the induced automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ of $FSS$ over $\kappa$ satisfies $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q \in N \iff Q \in N$ for every place $Q$, and for $Q \notin N$ one has $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_Q) = D_{R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau \cdot Q}$, where $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,D = \{P : \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D\}$.
--
--   `hUniq` (uniqueness of the packages): for every $Q \notin N$ and every quadruple $(S, \varphi, \chi_0, D)$ of the same shape satisfying the same fourteen clauses, one has $D = D_Q$ and $S = S_Q$ as sets, and $\chi_0$ agrees with $\chi_{0,Q}$ on $S$.
--
--   `hdl` (Drinfeld identification of the reduced field): for every $(\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain, and every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and an isomorphism $e$ of $\kappa$-algebras from $FSS$ onto $\mathrm{DrinfeldCurve.quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ (the fixed field in the Drinfeld function field of the subgroup generated by the actions of $C_s$) such that $\mathrm{Nat.card}\,C_s = 2 \cdot \mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, the latter being $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q\,(s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M'))$ divided by $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\,M'\,s$, and such that $e$ intertwines the level action with the Drinfeld action: for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, given that $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, one has, for all $x \in FSS$, that $e(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1})\,x)$ equals the image of $e(x)$ under $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$, both sides being read inside the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{drinfeldFunctionField}\,q\,\kappa$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the conclusion asserts the existence of a natural number $n$ and a family $z : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to FSS$ such that: first, each $z_i$ lies in the valuation subring of every place $Q \notin N$; and second, every $f \in FSS$ lying in the valuation subring of every place $Q \notin N$ belongs to the $\kappa$-subalgebra $\mathrm{Algebra.adjoin}\,\kappa\,(\mathrm{Set.range}\,z)$ generated by the $z_i$. Thus the statement gives finitely many functions, themselves regular away from the $q+1$ places of $N$, generating a $\kappa$-algebra containing all functions regular away from $N$; it is a containment, not an equality of rings.
--
--   This is the $q = 3$ case, under the auxiliary rigid-level guard provided by a prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the finite-generation step in the analysis of the supersingular part of the stable reduction of the modular curve at $q$: the component attached to a supersingular place $s$ is identified with a quotient of the Drinfeld curve, whose affine ring away from the $q+1$ ends is finitely generated over the residue field. It feeds the construction of an affine chart in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_generators_regular_off_ends_of_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.supersingularProlongation_exists_generators_regular_off_ends_of_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
